      "description": "Why work here? | Kingston University London Skip to main content Please enable JavaScript in your web browser to get the best experience. Please enable JavaScript in your web browser to get the best experience. Search Search term Search Course list Clearing Open days Future Skills Read the Future Skills report 2025 Kingston University is leading the way in the delivery of Future Skills in the United Kingdom. Our latest Future Skills report, launched at the House of Commons, is informed by extensive research. The report explores the skills most valued by employers in graduates, skills that are vital to drive innovation and boost economic growth. Clearing Study Experience Research Collaborate About us Search Menu Clearing Clearing Clearing Clearing Courses in Clearing Order a Clearing guide Study Study Study Study Search all courses Undergraduate Undergraduate Undergraduate Undergraduate courses How to apply Clearing 2026 Information for parents, carers and supporters Study abroad Join our undergraduate mailing list Postgraduate Postgraduate Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Professional placement Join our postgraduate mailing list Foundation Foundation Foundation Foundation courses Degree apprenticeships Degree apprenticeships Degree apprenticeships Degree apprenticeship courses Short courses Short courses Short courses Short courses Online courses International students International students International students International admissions timeline Visas, immigration and CAS Confirmation of Acceptance for Studies (CAS) Direct application for international students Country-specific information English language entry requirements English language programmes Study Abroad Programme Erasmus and European Exchange Pre-arrival information Arriving in the UK Fees and funding Fees and funding Fees and funding Understanding your fee status Undergraduate finance Postgraduate finance International student finance Welcome and Induction 2026 Welcome and Induction 2026 Welcome and Induction 2026 Enrolment Graduation Graduation Graduation Graduation ceremonies Certificates and transcripts Order a guide Order a guide Order a guide Undergraduate guide Postgraduate guide Experience Experience Experience Experience Commuting to Kingston University? Kingston Connect Adobe Creative Campus Outreach at Kingston University Student life Student life Student life Chat to our Student Ambassadors Achieving at Kingston University What our international students say Research student experiences Kingston Students' Union Mentee and mentor experiences Our campuses Our campuses Our campuses Penrhyn Road Kingston Hill Knights Park Roehampton Vale Visit the right campus Sports clubs, facilities and activities Accommodation Accommodation Accommodation Halls of residence Private student accommodation Equality, diversity and inclusion Equality, diversity and inclusion Equality, diversity and inclusion Inclusive curriculum Gender Equality Plan Athena Swan Diversity and inclusion calendar Elevate careers programme Transparency Women in STEM Careers and employability Student support Student support Student support Academic support Cost of living support Disability and mental health support Health and wellbeing IT support for students Head Start programme for undergraduates Estranged students Mature students Students who are parents Young adult carers Care leaver support Faith and spirituality Research Research Research Research Research degrees Knowledge Exchange and Research Institutes Knowledge Exchange and Research Institutes Knowledge Exchange and Research Institutes Behaviour, Business, and Policy KERI Cyber, Engineering and Digital Technologies KERI Design, Arts and Creative Practice KERI Health, Education and Society KERI Research facilities Case studies Collaborate Collaborate Collaborate Collaborate Services for business Services for business Services for business Knowledge Exchange Training and professional development Work with students and graduates Recruit Kingston University talent Intellectual property and commercialisation Degree Apprenticeships - Information for Employers Knowledge Transfer Partnerships Our partnerships Volunteer at Kingston University Facilities and venue hire Support us Support us Support us Why give? Legacy giving Community of donors Supporting student success through Future Skills Alumni Alumni Alumni Your alumni community Community engagement About us About us About us About us Contact us Future Skills Strategy and values Governance News Events Our academic faculties Our academic faculties Our academic faculties Kingston School of Art Business and Social Sciences Health, Science, Social Care and Education Engineering, Computing and the Environment Our staff Jobs Student login: Canvas My Kingston Read the Future Skills report 2025 Kingston University is leading the way in the delivery of Future Skills in the United Kingdom. Our latest Future Skills report, launched at the House of Commons, is informed by extensive research. The report explores the skills most valued by employers in graduates, skills that are vital to drive innovation and boost economic growth. Home About us Jobs at Kingston University Why work here? Working at Kingston University comes with a range of benefits. Find out everything you need to know to make the most of being a member of staff here. Why Kingston University is a great place to work More than just a job Kingston University offers a vibrant, supportive workplace that values its staff at the heart of its success. Whether you're an academic professional or administrative expert, you'll find opportunities to advance your career while enjoying a sense of community. The University prioritises personal development with tailored training programmes, sponsorship for further qualifications and membership funding for professional bodies. Staff benefit from flexible transport options, discounted goods and services, and access to cutting-edge resources like the Learning and Teaching Enhancement Centre. The University also prides itself on working responsibly with the environment and fostering a culture of sustainable practices. Set in a beautiful location near London, our staff also contribute to meaningful initiatives in the local community, promoting education and inclusivity. Join us and be part of an institution that values innovation, collaboration and growth. I value working at Kingston University because of its inclusive and collegial atmosphere, where collaboration and diversity are celebrated. It’s inspiring to be part of a community that empowers staff to make a meaningful impact on every student’s journey. Dipa Kamdar, Senior Lecturer in Pharmacy Practice Staff benefits Kingston University staff make us who we are – so it’s only right to give back. Working here gives you access to a wide range of benefits and perks. Benefits include an excellent pension scheme, generous holiday allowance, great development opportunities (see below for further information), University bus transport around Kingston and the local area and access to excellent campus facilities. Read our 'Benefits of working at Kingston University' booklet to find out more. Benefits of working at Kingston University (PDF) Opportunities for professional growth Our staff are the most important resource we have. We are committed to fostering your career development through robust support systems, professional training, and networking opportunities. Our inclusive workplace culture ensures equal opportunities for all, enabling staff to grow in their roles while maintaining work-life balance. At Kingston University, you will benefit from initiatives designed to help you excel, including: Induction programmes Feel at home thanks to comprehensive introductions. Once you start at Kingston University, you will automatically be invited to one of our 'welcome to Kingston' events. These interactive sessions offer you the opportunity to understand the University better and meet other new staff. Training and development We offer our Course Fee Waiver Scheme, which encourages the development of all eligible staff for successful completion of undergraduate and postgraduate courses taught at Kingston University, which are relevant to their job. Staff can apply for the scheme to attend one credit-bearing degree course at any one time without having to pay the associated tuition fees. Community volunteering opportunities Engage with our local community to give back to Kingston. Our staff and students are active in the local community, offering 3,500 hours of service to good causes each year through our award-winning volunteering scheme. We also have an extensive school visiting programme, offering educational support and encouraging local children to aim for university, particularly those from families with no previous experience of higher education. Pathways to progression Benefit from clear structures for advancement within your field. You can also seek guidance for experienced colleagues through our mentorship opportunities. At Kingston University, we are committed to nurturing leadership at every level. Our development programmes empower individuals to lead in line with our four core values: Ambitious, Inclusive, Innovative and Enterprising. Through tailored learning experiences, collaborative networks and practical tools, we help leaders unlock their potential and drive positive impact across the University and beyond. Help us to maintain high standards Make a valuable contribution to the establishment of higher education studies as a discipline in its own right. Join the Learning and Teaching Enhancement Centre (LTEC) to encourage continued study. Enhance your health We put your wellbeing first, with plenty of events and initiatives to support your health. You can take advantage of: Support from our Occupational Health team Generous occupation sick pay if you’re unwell Access to a free, confidential and 24/7 Employee Assistance Programme (EAP) Discounted membership at Lifestyle Fitness* *Lifestyle Fitness is our newly refurbished fitness centre located on the Penrhyn Road campus, providing cardio facilities, resistance machines and a free weights zone. Working at Kingston University has given me a fantastic opportunity to grow both personally and professionally. The supportive environment, development opportunities and strong ‘team’ relationships make it a great place to build a fulfilling and rewarding career. Joanna Kaplita, Head of ERP Systems Travel seamlessly We offer travel season ticket loans of up to £10,000 to help you ease the cost of commuting. Get a tax-free bicycle and safety equipment through our partnership with Cyclescheme Ltd. Catch the intersite bus service, which runs 50 weeks of the year. View the intersite bus timetable Extra perks Park your car We have limited parking available, but all University car parks are reserved for staff during core working hours You must have a registered valid electronic parking permit to park on site External visitors can book free parking at the main receptions on each site Get money off Our fantastic Benefits StaffSpace pages and the Smart Spending App bring all the benefits available to staff into one place. Benefits include discounts and cashback deals with hundreds of retailers and providers. Tap into free software Download Microsoft software (including Microsoft Office) to use at work and at home. Access extra support Access a wide range of free services and support for you and the people you live with through our Employee Assistance Programme. Keep in touch after retirement Join the Kingston University Retired Staff Association (KURSA) to stay in touch with fellow staff members. Take part in social activities, meet new people and more. Got a question about working at Kingston University? Call us on +44 (0)20 8417 3118 or send us an email. Email the HR team Stay in touch Instagram LinkedIn Facebook X YouTube TikTok Threads Contact us Student policies Terms and conditions Accessibility statement Freedom of information Statement on modern slavery Privacy, data protection and cookies Kingston University, Holmwood House, Grove Crescent, Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Tel:   +44 (0)20 8417 9000 Copyright © Kingston University London, 2026. By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
