    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/head-of-department-of-architecture-and-landscape-associate-professor-617908.html": {
      "title": "Head of Department of Architecture and Landscape & Associate Professor",
      "description": "Head of Department of Architecture and Landscape & Associate Professor (4930) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Head of Department of Architecture and Landscape & Associate Professor Faculty/Directorate Kingston School of Art School/Function School of Arts Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Knights Park Actual hours 37 Salary from 60,996.00 Salary to 70,239.00 Posted Date 21/08/2026 Closing Date 20/09/2026 Ref No 4930 Documents Candidate Pack - Associate Professor (PDF , 10722.76kb) Job Description (PDF , 462.04kb) The Role Shape the future of Architecture and Landscape at Kingston School of Art. Kingston School of Art is seeking an outstanding academic leader to join us as Associate Professor in Architecture and Landscape, serving as Head of Department for an initial four-year period. This is a permanent academic position, subject to probation, with the expectation that the successful candidate will return to standard departmental responsibilities following their period as Head of Department. This is an exciting opportunity to lead a vibrant, ambitious and interdisciplinary department and to play a key role in shaping the future of Architecture and Landscape at Kingston School of Art. As a member of the School Leadership Team, you will work closely with senior colleagues to translate School, Faculty and University priorities into meaningful action, driving excellence in student experience, academic quality, research, knowledge exchange and external engagement. As Head of Department, you will provide strategic, academic and operational leadership for Architecture and Landscape, ensuring an outstanding student experience and fostering a culture of innovation, inclusion and academic excellence. Alongside your leadership responsibilities, you will maintain an active academic profile appropriate to Associate Professor level through teaching, research, professional practice and/or knowledge exchange activity. The Person We are looking for a collaborative, credible and inspiring academic leader with the vision, judgement and experience to lead change and support colleagues to thrive. You will have a strong understanding of the contemporary landscape of architectural and design education, with the ability to build on the Department's strengths while identifying and developing new opportunities for growth, collaboration and impact. You will be adept at building strong relationships across the University and with professional, industry and external partners, aligning departmental priorities with wider strategic ambitions. You will also bring the ability to manage resources effectively, including people, budgets, workload and specialist learning and studio spaces. We are particularly interested in candidates who can demonstrate a strong academic and professional profile alongside the leadership capability to take Architecture and Landscape into its next phase of development. This is an opportunity to shape not only the future of the Department, but also its contribution to the distinctive, practice-led and interdisciplinary culture of Kingston School of Art. Applicants will be required to demonstrate that they meet the Kingston University standards in learning and teaching, and research.  By the end of the probation period, you must have achieved the relevant level of UKPSF recognition (if this has not already been obtained). For those new to teaching, this will be through our accredited Introduction to Learning and Teaching and for those experienced in teaching, through our Kingston Academic Practice Standards Framework. ’ The successful candidate will demonstrate: Strategic leadership and vision, with the ability to lead the Department through change and identify opportunities for its future development. Strong people and management skills, with experience of leading diverse academic teams and managing staff, budgets, workload and specialist resources. Academic and professional credibility, with a strong record in teaching, research, knowledge exchange and/or professional practice relevant toArchitecture and Landscape. Commitment to an outstanding student experience, supporting student achievement, progression, belonging and academic development. Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work collaboratively across the University and develop productive relationships with professional, industry and cultural partners. A commitment to inclusion, innovation and collegiality, creating an environment in which staff and students can thrive. The vision and judgement to enhance the Department's profile and impact, strengthening its distinctive contribution to Kingston School of Art and its national and international reputation. The Faculty Kingston School of Art (KSA) has a strong heritage. Since its origins in the late 19th century it has established an exceptional reputation and become one of the UK's leading art and design educational institutions. The Faculty combines a dedication to creative risk-taking, innovation and experimentation with a commitment to working with numerous local, national and global partners and collaborators to lead and shape the future of the creative and cultural industries. As an Art School within a university, KSA fuses the benefits of an art and design-focused identity with the ability to be at the forefront of exciting cross-disciplinary developments in diverse areas such as health, business, engineering and the humanities and social sciences. Ranked in the top five per cent of the world for art and design education by QS Top Universities, KSA produces globally celebrated alumni, high performing courses, impactful research performance and regularly achieves industry and student awards while engaging with the latest thinking from industry practitioners. The Faculty works with leading brands and institutions forging exciting partnerships with organisations like the ICA, the Design Museum and the BFI. More recently, the Faculty has expanded its international presence through partnerships with the Indian Institute of Art and Design and the Pratt Institute in Brooklyn, America. With a wide variety of disciplines taught within the Faculty, KSA offers opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaboration in research and teaching - providing both exceptional choice for students and a stimulating environment for academics in the creative fields. Further information This is a full time (37 hours per week), permanent position with a starting salary of £60,996 per annum. There is an additional responsibilities allowance for the duration of tenure as Head of Department of £6000 per annum. Interviews are expected to be held in person on Tuesday 20th October 2026. For informal enquiries about the role, please contact Dr Fan Carter, head of School of Arts, KSA. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
