    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/senior-technician-in-chemistry-pharmacy-simulation-618365.html": {
      "title": "Senior Technician in Chemistry, Pharmacy & Simulation",
      "description": "Senior Technician in Chemistry, Pharmacy & Simulation  (4937) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Senior Technician in Chemistry, Pharmacy & Simulation Faculty/Directorate Faculty of Health, Science, Social Care & Education School/Function Faculty General (HSSCE) Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Penrhyn Road Actual hours 37 Salary from 39,407.00 Salary to 43,835.00 Posted Date 28/08/2026 Closing Date 22/09/2026 Ref No 4937 Documents Candidate Pack (PDF , 9919.68kb) Job Description (PDF , 197.49kb) The Role The role provides practical and operational technical support to the Faculty of Health, Science, Social Care and Education (HSSCE), supporting the Departments of Chemistry and Pharmacy and the School of Nursing across two local campus sites. The role will contribute to the effective delivery of teaching, student projects and research activities. The post holder will support the Assistant Technical Officer (ATO), and the day-to-day operation of the departments, including assisting with the supervision of junior technical staff, providing technical support and laboratory cover within Chemistry and preparing, setting up and dismantling practical classes in the Pharmaceutics laboratories. They will also deliver a range of practical sessions to students studying Pharmaceutical Science and Pharmacy. Another key aspect of the role is providing technical support for simulation-based learning within the Schools of Nursing and Pharmacy. This will include assisting junior technical staff with the delivery of simulation activities, setting up and dismantling equipment for teaching and assessment, resolving technical issues, and supporting the introduction and development of new simulation technologies designed to enhance the student learning experience. The postholder will work collaboratively with academic and technical colleagues and a wide range of stakeholders, providing reliable day-to-day support to ensure the smooth, safe and effective delivery of teaching, learning and assessment activities. Please see the job description for more details. The Person The successful candidate will ideally have experience in some or all of these areas, alongside a Chemistry Degree. The role is based across two local university campuses, so a flexible approach to working across both sites is essential. An inter-campus bus service is available to support travel between locations. As well as a Degree in Chemistry and laboratory experience you will have good problem-solving skills and be confident working with emerging and future technologies in the field of simulated learning. Health and Safety knowledge is essential for the role with ongoing training provided with the post. This is an exciting opportunity to develop and expand your existing technical skills through ongoing training and hands-on experience, while working closely with two teams across the respective campuses. Reporting to the Assistant Technical Officer on a day-to-day basis and working under the direction of the Simulation Manager whilst in our Nursing Department, you will play a key role in supporting students and academic staff throughout their practical teaching and learning activities. The Faculty The Faculty offers wide ranging practice-based education and training programmes across nursing, health science, midwifery, social care and teaching which are informed by high quality and impactful research. We have a successful track record in public and service user engagement and developing knowledge transfer partnerships and other enterprise activities. The Faculty’s professional administration and support teams work together to ensure business and support services are effective, efficient and sustainable in meeting the needs of our students, staff, stakeholders and areas of work. Further information This is a full time, permanent position with a starting salary of £39,407 per annum. Interviews are expected to be held on Tuesday 29 September 2026. For informal enquiries, please contact Mr Daren Chapman , Technical Officer. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
