    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/hr-mi-systems-partner-617459.html": {
      "title": "HR MI & Systems Partner",
      "description": "HR MI & Systems Partner (4924) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions HR MI & Systems Partner Faculty/Directorate Finance, Infrastructure and Human Resources School/Function Human Resources Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Penrhyn Road Actual hours 37 Salary from 50,160.00 Salary to 59,306.00 Posted Date 11/08/2026 Closing Date 14/09/2026 Ref No 4924 Documents Benefits Booklet (PDF , 23686.17kb) Candidate Pack (PDF , 10784.32kb) Job Description (Word , 260.44kb) The Role We are seeking a dedicated HR Management Information & Systems Partner to provide a leading HR management information service. This role focuses on improving the quality and accessibility of workforce data, supporting HR in optimising systems, and delivering high-quality data products for strategic decision-making. The successful candidate will collaborate with HR teams and stakeholders to enhance data capabilities, aligning with the Town House Strategy and People Plan. Key Responsibilities: Support HR teams with access and interpretation of complex data sets. Plan and deliver the annual HESA Staff data return, ensuring compliance with changing requirements. Continuously improve the People Dashboard report for leadership teams. Assist in delivering Public Sector Equality Duty and Pay Gap reports. Respond to external requests for HR data, including FOI and SARs Deliver tailored workforce data products to facilitate decision-making. Lead as the HR data protection champion and ensure data quality and integrity. Develop tools and processes for continuous improvement in HR data management Directorate/Function The HR Directorate provides the strategy and infrastructure to enable Kingston University to achieve its core purpose through its people. The successful candidate will be joining an experienced and talented team of HR professionals who deliver HR operations, strategy and design for it’s 3k strong employee base. Our professionals give high level support across the University along with responding to day to day queries from all areas and staff. In addition, they ensure our policies and procedures provide suitable frameworks to enable staff to operate successfully during their employment at Kingston University. Together we aim to enable Kingston University to recruit, develop and motivate staff, so that we all contribute to the University’s success. Further information This is a full time, permanent position with a starting salary of £50,160 Interviews are expected to be held in person on the 1st October 2026. For further information about this opportunity, visit: https://www.morganhunt.com/jobs/search/167627-HR-Management-Information-Systems-Partner For an informal conversation about the role, please contact our recruitment partners at Morganhunt fraser.young@morganhunt.com Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply Now Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applica